    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_a7008509",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: whoevers_photoshopped_this_is_a_huge_jerk; hasOverallIntent: Abusive; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a woman with a shocked expression surrounded by multiple hands pointing at her. The text reads 'whoever photoshopped this is a huge jerk.' The overall intent is to express anger and blame toward the person who created or edited the image, using a confrontational and accusatory tone. The visual of multiple hands pointing at the woman amplifies the sense of being targeted and criticized. While the meme is directed at the creator of the image rather than a specific individual or group based on protected characteristics, it is abusive in nature because it uses aggressive language and imagery to shame and attack the person responsible for the image. The intent is to publicly shame and insult the creator, which can be seen as a form of online harassment or cyberbullying, even if the target is not a specific community or identity group. The meme does not contain any toxic content targeting protected characteristics, but its abusive tone and intent to shame the creator make it fall under the 'Abusive' category.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_c81d718c"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
